          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            What is called
            %em global equivariant homotopy theory
            is a variant of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"} equivariant cohomology
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            where
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
            are equipped with
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-actions"} infinity-actions
            “for all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+groups"} compact Lie groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            at once”, or more generally for a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+family"} global family
          %p
            Sometimes this is referred to just as “global homotopy theory”, leaving the equivariance implicit. There is also a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilization"} stable
            version involving
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
            equipped with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-actions"} infinity-actions
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+equivariant+stable+homotopy+theory"} global equivariant stable homotopy theory
          %p
            More precisely, the
            %em global equivariant homotopy category
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            (or else its
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} homotopy category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-presheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi PSh
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Orb
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh_\infty(Orb)
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+orbit+category"} global orbit category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Orb
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Orb
            (
            %a{:href => "#HenriquesGepner07"}> Henriques-Gepner 07, section 1.3
            ), regarded as an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
          %p
            Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Orb
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Orb
            has as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+groups"} compact Lie groups
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categorical+hom-spaces"} (∞,1)-categorical hom-spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Orb
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Orb(G,H) \coloneqq \Pi [\mathbf{B}G, \mathbf{B}H]
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization+of+cohesive+infinity-groupoids"} fundamental (∞,1)-groupoid
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+groupoid"} topological groupoid
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+homomorphisms"} group homomorphisms
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugation"} conjugations
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p
            We follow (
            %a{:href => "#Rezk14"}> Rezk 14
            ). Beware that the terminology there differs slightly but crucially in some places from (
            %a{:href => "#HenriquesGepner07"}> Henriques-Gepner 07
            ). Whatever terminology one uses, the following are the key definitions.
          %p
            The following is the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+equivariant+indexing+category"} global equivariant indexing category
          #GlobalIndexingCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Glo
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Glo
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              whose
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                  are
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+groups"} compact Lie groups
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categorical+hom-spaces"} (∞,1)-categorical hom-spaces
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Glo
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi G
                        %mo ,
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Glo(G,H)
                  are the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realizations"} geometric realizations
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoid"} Lie groupoid
                  of smooth functors and smooth
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Top
                          %mn ∞
                          %mi Grpd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                          %mo ,
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi H
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top\infty Grpd(\mathbf{B}G, \mathbf{B}H)
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Rezk14"}> Rezk 14, 2.1
            )
          .num_defn
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Equivalent models for the global indexing category, def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GlobalIndexingCategory"}
              include the category “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi O
                      %mi gl
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O_{gl}
              ” of (
              %a{:href => "#May90"}> May 90
              ). Another variant is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi O
                      %mi gl
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{O}_{gl}
              of (
              %a{:href => "#Schwede13"}> Schwede 13
              ).
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Rezk14"}> Rezk 14, 2.4, 2.5
            )
          %p
            The following is the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+orbit+category"} global orbit category
          #GlobalOrbitCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Orb
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Glo
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Orb \longrightarrow Glo
            %p
              for the non-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} full
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} sub-(∞,1)-category
              of the global indexing category, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GlobalIndexingCategory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injection"} injective
              group homomorphisms.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Rezk14"}> Rezk14, 4.5
            )
          %p
            The following defines the
            %em global equivariant homotopy theory
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Glo
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh_\infty(Glo)
          #GlobalEquivariantHomotopyTopos.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi Glo
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Glo
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Top_{Glo} \coloneqq PSh_\infty(Glo)
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-presheaves
              (an
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Glo
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Glo
              of def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GlobalIndexingCategory"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔹
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Glo
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Glo
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{B} \;\colon\; Glo \longrightarrow PSh_\infty(Glo)
            %p
              for the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Yoneda+embedding"} (∞,1)-Yoneda embedding
            %p Similarly write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi Orb
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Orb
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Top_{Orb} \coloneqq PSh_\infty(Orb)
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-presheaves
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+orbit+category"} global orbit category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Orb
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Orb
              of def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GlobalOrbitCategory"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔹
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Orb
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Orb
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{B} \;\colon\; Orb \longrightarrow PSh_\infty(Orb)
            %p
              for its
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Yoneda+embedding"} (∞,1)-Yoneda embedding
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Rezk14"}> Rezk 14, 3.1 and 4.5
            )
          %p
            The following recovers the ordinary (“local”)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+theory"} equivariant homotopy theory
            of a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+group"} compact Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            (“of
            = succeed "-spaces\u201D)." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          #LocalEquivariantHomotopyTheory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+group"} compact Lie group
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mi Top
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Orb
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi 𝔹
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    G Top \coloneqq PSh_\infty(Orb)/\mathbb{B}G
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} slice (∞,1)-topos
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Orb
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh_\infty(Orb)
              over the image of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              under the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Yoneda+embedding"} (∞,1)-Yoneda embedding
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GlobalEquivariantHomotopyTopos"}
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#Rezk14"}> Rezk 14, 1.5
            ). Depending on axiomatization this is either a definition or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elmendorf%27s+theorem"} Elmendorf's theorem
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+theory"} equivariant homotopy theory
            for more on this.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#cohesion Cohesion
          %p
            For more see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion+of+global-+over+G-equivariant+homotopy+theory"} cohesion of global- over G-equivariant homotopy theory
          #CohesionOfGlobalEquivariantHomotopyTheory.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The global equivariant homotopy theory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Glo
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh_\infty(Glo)
              of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GlobalEquivariantHomotopyTopos"}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
              over the canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} base (∞,1)-topos
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            %p
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section+geometric+morphism"} global section geometric morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Glo
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\Delta \dashv \Gamma)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    PSh_\infty(Glo)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\infty Grpd
            %p
              is given (as for all (∞,1)-presheaf (∞,1)-toposes) by the
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+image"} direct image
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
              functor being the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy limit
              over the opposite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-site"} (∞,1)-site
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi X
                    %mo ≃
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo ←
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Glo
                      %mi op
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma X \simeq \underset{\leftarrow}{\lim}(Glo^{op}\stackrel{X}{\to} \infty Grpd)
            %p
              and the
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+%E2%88%9E-stack"} constant ∞-stack
              functor literally assigning constant presheaves:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi G
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi S
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Delta S \colon G \mapsto S
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} full and faithful (∞,1)-functor
            %p
              Moreover,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
              has a further
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
              which preserves
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+products"} finite products
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              has a further
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∇
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Rezk14"}> Rezk 14, 5.1
            )
          %p
            More in detail, the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape modality
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+modality"} flat modality
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sharp+modality"} sharp modality
            of this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesion
            of the global equivariant homotopy theory has the following description.
          %h3#relation_between_global_and_local_equivariant_homotopy_theory Relation between global and local equivariant homotopy theory
          %p
            Some aspects of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion+of+global-+over+G-equivariant+homotopy+theory"} cohesion of global- over G-equivariant homotopy theory
          #InclusionOfGSpacesInTheGlobalTheory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+group"} compact Lie group
              define an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi G
                    %mi Top
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Glo
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\delta_G \;\colon\; G Top \longrightarrow PSh_\infty(Glo)
            %p
              sending a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+G-space"} topological G-space
              to the he presheaf which sends a group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+groupoid"} topological groupoid
              of maps from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}H
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X//G
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi H
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi H
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\delta_G(X)\;\colon\; H \mapsto \Pi( [\mathbf{B}H, X//G] )
                    \\,.
            %p
              Observe that by def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GlobalEquivariantHomotopyTopos"}
              this gives
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi 𝔹
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_G(\ast) \simeq \mathbb{B}G
              and so
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_G
              induces a functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi G
                    %mi Top
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi G
                    %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo *
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Orb
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi 𝔹
                    %mi G
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi δ
                          %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Glo
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi 𝔹
                    %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Delta_G \;\colon\; G Top \simeq G Top/\ast \simeq PSh_\infty(Orb)/\mathbb{B}G \stackrel{\delta_G}{\longrightarrow} PSh_\infty(Glo)/\mathbb{B}G
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Rezk14"}> Rezk 14, 3.2
            )
          #OrdinaryQuotientAndHomotopyQuotientViaCohesion.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (ordinary
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
                via equivariant cohesion)
            %p
              On a
              = succeed "-space" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi G
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in G Top
              included via def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InclusionOfGSpacesInTheGlobalTheory"}
              into the global equivariant homotopy theory,
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape modality
                  of def.
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CohesionOfGlobalEquivariantHomotopyTheory"}
                  produces the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
                  of the ordinary
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
                  of the
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Π
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi δ
                          %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\Pi(\delta_G(X)) \simeq \vert X/G \vert
                        \\,,
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+modality"} flat modality
                  of def.
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CohesionOfGlobalEquivariantHomotopyTheory"}
                  produces the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
                  of the
                  = succeed "/" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coinvariants"} homotopy coinvariants
                  of the
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"}> ∞-action
                  )
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi δ
                          %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\Gamma(\delta_G(X)) \simeq \vert X//G \vert
                        \\,,
            %p
              In particular then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/points-to-pieces+transform"} points-to-pieces transform
              of general
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesion
              yields the comparison map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\vert X//G \vert
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\vert X/G \vert
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Rezk14"}> Rezk 14, 5.1
            )
          #CohesionOnLocalSlice.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              any
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+group"} compact Lie group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesion
              of the global equivariant homotopy theory, prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CohesionOfGlobalEquivariantHomotopyTheory"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} slice (∞,1)-toposes
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Glo
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi 𝔹
                    %mi G
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi PSh
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Orb
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi 𝔹
                    %mi G
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi G
                    %mi Top
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    PSh_\infty(Glo)/\mathbb{B}G
                    \\longrightarrow
                    PSh_\infty(Orb)/\mathbb{B}G \simeq G Top
                    \\,,
            %p
              hence to cohesion over the “local”
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+theory"} equivariant homotopy theory
            %p
              The inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_G
              is that of def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InclusionOfGSpacesInTheGlobalTheory"}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Rezk14"}> Rezk 14, 5.3
            )
          %h3#relation_to_topological_stacks_and_orbispaces Relation to topological stacks and orbispaces
          %blockquote
            %p under construction
          %p
            By the main theorem of (
            %a{:href => "#HenriquesGepner07"}> Henriques-Gepner 07
            ) the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-presheaves
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+orbit+category"} global orbit category
            are equivalently “cellular”
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+stacks"} topological stacks
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+groupoids"} topological groupoids
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbispaces"}> orbispaces
            ”), we might write this as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ETopGrpd
                    %mi cell
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi PSh
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Orb
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  ETopGrpd^{cell} = PSh_\infty(Orb)
                  \\,.
          %p
            (As such the global equivariant homotopy theory should be similar to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ETop%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ETop∞Grpd
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            such that it sends a topological
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            acting on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(X)//\Pi(G)
          %p
            The central theorem of (
            %a{:href => "#Rezk14"}> Rezk 14
            ) (using a slightly different definition than
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#HenriquesGepner07"} Henriques-Gepner 07
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi PSh
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Orb
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh_\infty(Orb)
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            producing homotopy quotients.
          %h3#relation_to_differentiable_stacks Relation to differentiable stacks
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} SepStk
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{SepStk}
            denote the
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separated+morphism"} separated
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+stacks"} differentiable stacks
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+map"} proper map
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} topology
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+covers"} open covers
            of stacks; we let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Shv
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} SepStk
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Shv}(\mathrm{SepStk})
            be the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-category"} ∞-category
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-sheaf"} sheaves of spaces
            %em homotopy invariant sheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Shv
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} htp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} SepStk
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Shv
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} SepStk
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Shv}^{\mathrm{htp}}(\mathrm{SepStk}) \subset \mathrm{Shv}(\mathrm{SepStk})
            be the full subcategory spanned by those sheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℱ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
            such that the map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℱ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔛
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℱ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔛
                  %mo ×
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}(\mathfrak{X}) \rightarrow \mathcal{F}(\mathfrak{X} \times \mathbb{R})
            induced by the projection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔛
                  %mo ×
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝔛
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{X} \times \mathbb{R} \rightarrow \mathfrak{X}
            is an equivalence for every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separated+morphism"} separated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+stack"} differentiable stack
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔛
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{X}
          %p
            Given
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a finite group, its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoid"} action groupoid
            lifts to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separated+morphism"} separated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+stack"} differentiable stack
            = succeed "," do
